1
00:00:02,252 --> 00:00:03,336
[PRECIOUS]
<i>How is she?</i>

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
<i>Still the same.</i>

3
00:00:04,629 --> 00:00:07,090
<i>She's still being pushy</i>
<i>with what she wants.</i>

4
00:00:07,173 --> 00:00:10,927
<i>She should be grateful she's not in jail.</i>

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:13,430
<i>She committed a huge crime.</i>

6
00:00:14,431 --> 00:00:15,473
<i>Crime?</i>

7
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:18,810
<i>Who do you think is really at fault here?</i>

8
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:21,563
<i>You're a mistress, Precious.</i>

9
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:23,565
<i>In the eyes of the law and God,</i>

10
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:25,191
<i>I'm still the wife.</i>

11
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:27,027
<i>You're just a mistress.</i>

12
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:29,863
<i>You are the real sinner!</i>

13
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:33,241
- [NURSE CALLING] <i>Police! Police!</i>
- [PRECIOUS GRUNTING]

14
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:35,952
<i>- Hey! Stop that!</i>
<i>- Stop it!</i>

15
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:38,955
<i>You're mine, Enrico! Just mine!</i>

16
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:40,582
<i>Come on.</i>

17
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:46,296
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

18
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:50,425
[THERAPIST]<i> She no longer</i>
<i>exhibits psychotic symptoms</i>

19
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:53,428
<i>or signs of mental incompetence.</i>

20
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,473
<i>What does that mean? What happens now?</i>

21
00:00:56,556 --> 00:00:58,433
<i>Once the court order is issued,</i>

22
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:00,852
<i>we'll put her back in the city jail.</i>

23
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:03,605
<i>She'll be held there</i>
<i>while her case is ongoing.</i>

24
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:07,859
<i>♪ It was way too much and way too fast ♪</i>

25
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:10,278
<i>♪ I can give you space ♪</i>

26
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:15,033
<i>♪ But don't be gone too long before ♪</i>

27
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,243
<i>♪ You'll hear me say ♪</i>

28
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:20,205
<i>♪ I swear, I gave you my best ♪</i>

29
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:24,417
<i>♪ Yeah, I gave it all to you ♪</i>

30
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:31,883
<i>♪ I know it hurts</i>
<i>Now was it worth the truth? ♪</i>

31
00:01:31,966 --> 00:01:35,678
<i>Wow! Boss, you've really leveled up!</i>

32
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:38,264
<i>Look at that. All those girls</i>
<i>are going crazy over you!</i>

33
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:42,143
<i>Meanwhile, I'm still trying</i>
<i>to find someone on LoveList.</i>

34
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:44,103
<i>- Really?</i>
<i>- Yeah. I matched with someone.</i>

35
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:45,897
<i>We went on a date.</i>

36
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,232
<i>Then she blocked me.</i>

37
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:50,068
<i>Maybe she just wasn't the one for you.</i>

38
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:52,112
<i>You know.</i>

39
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:54,155
<i>You'll find the right one.</i>

40
00:01:55,323 --> 00:01:56,866
<i>Do you really believe that, boss?</i>

41
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,660
<i>That whole "take it easy" thing?</i>

42
00:01:58,743 --> 00:02:01,204
<i>You took it way too easy yourself,</i>
<i>and you lost the one for you.</i>

43
00:02:01,996 --> 00:02:04,958
<i>Billy said she wants to</i>
<i>keep our friendship.</i>

44
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:06,835
<i>And I agree.</i>

45
00:02:07,418 --> 00:02:12,590
<i>You know, sometimes,</i>
<i>friendship lasts longer.</i>

46
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:17,428
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:22,058
<i>I'll expedite Mariela's clinical diagnosis</i>

48
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:24,352
<i>so I can submit it to the court.</i>

49
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:28,690
<i>I think it'll give us strong grounds</i>
<i>for getting our marriage annulled.</i>

50
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:30,441
- [BILLY]<i> Dad?</i>
- [KNOCKS ON DOOR]

51
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:34,070
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,405
<i>Auntie?</i>

53
00:02:37,115 --> 00:02:38,533
<i>What happened to your face?</i>

54
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:43,746
<i>Oh.</i>

55
00:02:45,415 --> 00:02:47,834
<i>I'll stay with your sister Bea</i>
<i>for a while, okay?</i>

56
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:50,253
<i>I'm going to miss you, Papa.</i>

57
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:52,130
<i>I'll miss you too.</i>

58
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:54,257
- [OLIVER] <i>Love you.</i>
- [ENRICO]<i> Love you.</i>

59
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:56,885
<i>Billy?</i>

60
00:02:56,968 --> 00:03:03,975
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:06,686
[LINE RINGS]

62
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:08,730
<i>Billy, where are you?</i>

63
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:11,232
<i>I'm just going to talk to Bea.</i>

64
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:13,443
<i>- Billy…</i>
<i>- This is about her mother.</i>

65
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:18,114
<i>This is exactly why that woman</i>
<i>can't be allowed to go free.</i>

66
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:20,408
<i>Billy, dear?</i>

67
00:03:20,491 --> 00:03:22,493
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

68
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:24,954
[CALL ENDS]

69
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:35,632
[BEA] I'm on my way there.

70
00:03:36,257 --> 00:03:37,675
Wait for me, okay?

71
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:44,766
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:55,944
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:04:56,963 --> 00:05:02,635
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:05:18,943 --> 00:05:22,030
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

75
00:05:22,113 --> 00:05:25,199
[CITY NOISE]

76
00:05:25,283 --> 00:05:28,578
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

77
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:46,471
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:51,392
[OUT OF SERVICE TONE]

79
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:09,952
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

80
00:06:10,995 --> 00:06:13,664
You know, I already pleaded with Billy.

81
00:06:13,748 --> 00:06:16,167
I almost begged for mercy.

82
00:06:17,293 --> 00:06:18,544
But it did nothing.

83
00:06:18,628 --> 00:06:21,464
That woman doesn't really care about me.

84
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:23,883
What about your father?

85
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:25,551
He's just like her.

86
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:28,846
[BEA] He also doesn't care
about me or my mother.

87
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:30,014
Now, Billy, on the other hand.

88
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:33,184
That's who he listens to.
Billy, Billy, Billy!

89
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:35,812
Fine, stick with Billy forever!

90
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:42,735
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

91
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:03,256
Caloy, just help me out here.

92
00:07:04,132 --> 00:07:07,927
Let's just break Mom out of the hospital.

93
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,347
Mm.

94
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:18,396
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

95
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:40,418
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:07:55,433 --> 00:08:02,398
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

97
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:13,117
Hey.

98
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:16,078
Come here for a second.
Just rest for a bit.

99
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,873
I already told you that
I can't rest, Caloy!

100
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:23,419
I already told you.
We need to think of a plan.

101
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:27,340
[BEA] We need to figure out

102
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:30,218
how to break her out of that hospital.

103
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:32,887
The problem is, it's not easy.

104
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:36,474
Planning it will be hard, especially since
they're about to send her back to prison.

105
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:38,643
[CALOY] Come here. Stop worrying about it.

106
00:08:39,977 --> 00:08:41,354
Just relax for a while.

107
00:08:41,437 --> 00:08:43,898
Let's have a drink.

108
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:47,318
What are you talking about?
I didn't come here to drink with you.

109
00:08:47,401 --> 00:08:49,737
[BEA] Caloy, help my mother.

110
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,990
[CALOY] Don't worry, okay?

111
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,951
I'll take care of everything.

112
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:59,747
We'll break your mother out.

113
00:09:01,123 --> 00:09:03,626
You know I'd do anything for you, right?

114
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:08,714
Because I love you so much.

115
00:09:08,798 --> 00:09:15,054
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

116
00:09:15,137 --> 00:09:17,265
Fine! I love you too.

117
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:21,686
You know it already.
I don't always have to say it, right?

118
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:26,065
Come here.

119
00:09:28,401 --> 00:09:29,735
[CALOY] Hug!

120
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:30,736
Huh?

121
00:09:31,612 --> 00:09:33,406
[CALOY] It's just a hug.

122
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:36,867
I don't like my baby getting stressed.

123
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:37,868
[CALOY] Come here.

124
00:09:37,952 --> 00:09:44,250
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:46,752
[CARDBOARD THUDS]

126
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:49,463
What was that?

127
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:50,631
[CARDBOARD THUDS]

128
00:09:55,553 --> 00:09:56,679
What was that noise?

129
00:09:56,762 --> 00:09:57,972
There's someone else here.

130
00:09:58,556 --> 00:09:59,682
[KNIFE SWISHES]

131
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:00,891
Let's move.

132
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:07,940
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:10:22,204 --> 00:10:24,040
[OUT OF SERVICE TONE]

134
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:30,630
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:10:38,095 --> 00:10:39,388
[LINE RINGING]

136
00:10:39,472 --> 00:10:40,931
[POLICE OFFICER] <i>NLEA Police Station.</i>

137
00:10:41,015 --> 00:10:41,974
Hello?

138
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,934
Hello, this is Billy Cariño.

139
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:46,520
I know where Carlos Toledo is hiding.

140
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:52,610
[BILLY] Sir. Sir, they are
on the eighth floor.

141
00:10:53,277 --> 00:10:54,779
Okay, men, move!

142
00:10:54,862 --> 00:11:01,535
- [THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

143
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:15,466
Santiago, search that area!

144
00:11:15,549 --> 00:11:18,469
Aguilar, Santos! Reyes!
Go over there! Move!

145
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:19,804
Move, move!

146
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:26,685
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

147
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:38,072
Dad, stop defending her.

148
00:11:38,155 --> 00:11:40,199
You weren't there to see it for yourself.

149
00:11:40,991 --> 00:11:43,702
Dear, why don't you go home for now?

150
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,913
Let me talk to your sister first.

151
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:48,999
[SCREEN DOOR SQUEAKS, THUDS]

152
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:50,918
[ENRICO] Bea.

153
00:11:51,001 --> 00:11:52,420
Where have you been?

154
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:57,091
[BEA] Um…

155
00:11:57,174 --> 00:12:01,011
You see, Pa…
My former employer?

156
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:04,098
Well, they called me
to help with something.

157
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:05,558
Are you kidding me?!
You're lying!

158
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:07,685
What's this, then?
Explain yourself!

159
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:12,106
- Look at this!
- [DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

160
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,695
B-Billy, he's obsessed with me.

161
00:12:18,362 --> 00:12:19,989
Pa, he's obsessed with me.

162
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:21,657
He was harassing me.

163
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,325
I was being harassed, Billy.

164
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:25,744
He told me that he'd hurt you
if I didn't meet up with him.

165
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,079
And I didn't want that to happen.

166
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,873
Don't try to pull one on me, okay?

167
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:31,584
Don't you dare mess with me!

168
00:12:34,253 --> 00:12:36,464
I'll make sure you go back
to prison, you witch.

169
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:37,840
- Billy! Billy!
- Billy!

170
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,467
- Billy, that's enough!
- What?!

171
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:42,428
Your sister already explained everything.

172
00:12:42,511 --> 00:12:44,472
I'll deal with Bea.

173
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,185
Seriously?

174
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:50,686
[HALF-SOBS]

175
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:52,146
Are you for real?!

176
00:12:56,358 --> 00:12:59,737
Are you seriously taking
that woman's side?

177
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:03,157
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:07,536
The proof is right here!

179
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:09,455
Fine.

180
00:13:12,666 --> 00:13:14,919
Then you and your daughter
can stick together.

181
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:22,468
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

182
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:34,146
I was right all along, Auntie.

183
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,773
Bea never changed.

184
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:36,899
And it's partly my fault.

185
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:39,818
I gave her the opportunity
to manipulate Dad.

186
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:41,737
I never should've given her
a second chance.

187
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:44,406
Billy, your father's
in a difficult position.

188
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:46,033
He's caught in the middle.

189
00:13:46,116 --> 00:13:48,744
You're both his children,
and he loves you both.

190
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,204
We're both his children,

191
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:52,414
but only one of us is a criminal.

192
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:56,544
Maybe your father feels that
he's partly to blame

193
00:13:56,627 --> 00:13:58,879
for Bea turning out this way.

194
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:01,465
Bea can think for herself, Auntie.

195
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:04,343
Everything she does,
every decision she makes,

196
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:07,012
is her own choice, not anyone else's.

197
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:10,307
Even conspiring with Caloy
is her decision.

198
00:14:10,391 --> 00:14:13,561
So if that man causes trouble
for our family again,

199
00:14:13,644 --> 00:14:16,063
Bea will be to blame for it.

200
00:14:16,146 --> 00:14:22,236
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:24,446
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [BREATH QUIVERS]

202
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:27,116
[EXHALES, SNIFFLING]

203
00:14:28,784 --> 00:14:30,327
I'm really sorry, Pa.

204
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:32,955
I'm sorry for meeting up with Caloy.

205
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,832
I was just worried for you, Pa.

206
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:36,792
I didn't want you to worry.

207
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,253
I was just concerned, Pa. That's all.

208
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,797
You shouldn't have done that!

209
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:44,884
It's dangerous to have
any contact with that man!

210
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:45,843
I know, Pa.

211
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:48,596
But like I said earlier,
I only did it to protect you.

212
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:53,267
I wanted to protect my half-siblings too,
and Auntie Precious.

213
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:54,935
That's all, Pa.

214
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:56,896
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

215
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:59,732
But Billy, Pa…

216
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,818
She might have me sent back to prison.

217
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,862
Pa, I don't want to go back.

218
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:06,655
I don't want to be locked up again.

219
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,616
I don't want to go back to prison, Pa.

220
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:12,369
Please talk to Billy.
I can't go through that again.

221
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:14,455
- [MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [BREATH QUIVERING]

222
00:15:14,538 --> 00:15:16,040
Pa, please.

223
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:17,082
Pa…

224
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,752
I don't want to go back to prison.

225
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:22,004
[BEA SNIFFLES]

226
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:24,632
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

227
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:33,182
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

228
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:34,224
[SIGHS IN RELIEF]

229
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,893
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

230
00:15:37,269 --> 00:15:39,772
[ATTY. GRANADO] <i>I spoke</i>
<i>with the investigating officers</i>

231
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:41,982
<i>who are handling the manhunt</i>
<i>for Carlos Toledo.</i>

232
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:45,110
I made it clear that we want to be
informed of any developments.

233
00:15:46,195 --> 00:15:49,239
Okay. About Bea,
I want to reopen the cases.

234
00:15:49,323 --> 00:15:51,825
If we have grounds to do it,
then let's move forward.

235
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:55,371
[ATTY. GRANADO] <i>Since her cases were</i>
<i>dismissed without prejudice,</i>

236
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:58,123
<i>we can still refile them</i>
<i>with the prosecutor.</i>

237
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:00,793
Those were only provisional dismissals,
not final ones.

238
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:03,504
We are still within the revival period.

239
00:16:03,587 --> 00:16:07,132
We will present a new, complete affidavit
along with additional evidence.

240
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:08,550
Okay, Attorney.

241
00:16:09,385 --> 00:16:11,261
I'm willing to go through
the process again.

242
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:15,265
And if at all possible,
expedite Mariela's transfer to prison.

243
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:18,602
Attorney, I want to see both of them
in the correctional facility.

244
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:20,938
[GRANADO] <i>Well, according to the police,</i>

245
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:23,273
<i>Mariela is scheduled</i>
<i>to be transferred tonight.</i>

246
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:29,613
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:39,456
[MUSIC ENDS]

248
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:41,834
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

249
00:16:42,459 --> 00:16:44,044
Just stay here. I'll figure something out.

250
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:45,838
Make sure you do, okay?

251
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:49,758
Because Billy won't listen
to me anymore, Caloy.

252
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:52,469
Even if I begged on my knees,

253
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:55,389
she wouldn't change her mind.

254
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,307
I know about her plan.

255
00:16:57,933 --> 00:16:59,768
She's going to send me
and my mother back to prison.

256
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:02,354
I'm sure of it,
and I don't want that to happen.

257
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:04,398
- I said I'll take care of it.
- You'll take care of it?

258
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,817
Caloy, you better make sure
nothing goes wrong.

259
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,360
Just trust me.

260
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:10,070
Where's my good luck kiss?

261
00:17:10,654 --> 00:17:12,239
Damn it, I'm serious!

262
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:14,033
You'll meet your mother soon.

263
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,576
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:17:15,659 --> 00:17:17,953
I'll get her out of there. Don't worry.

265
00:17:20,664 --> 00:17:22,332
I know you're tired.

266
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:26,545
You're tired of fighting, aren't you?

267
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:30,049
I know that.

268
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:34,178
When your mother and I get back,
we're leaving this place.

269
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:37,389
I'll take you as far away as I can.

270
00:17:38,223 --> 00:17:39,641
Far away from all this chaos.

271
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:41,310
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

272
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:42,644
I'll hold you to that.

273
00:17:42,728 --> 00:17:44,772
- Promise me, Caloy.
- I will.

274
00:17:46,398 --> 00:17:47,524
You should go now.

275
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,112
Just go.

276
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:53,614
Take this seriously.

277
00:17:55,365 --> 00:18:01,580
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

278
00:18:01,663 --> 00:18:03,457
Here are the transfer documents, Doc.

279
00:18:08,545 --> 00:18:11,507
This is the patient's medical clearance,

280
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:13,801
including the
fit-to-transfer certification

281
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:16,762
and her medication schedule.

282
00:18:17,554 --> 00:18:19,014
Um, Mariela.

283
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:21,934
The police will be taking over from here.

284
00:18:22,851 --> 00:18:24,561
Ma'am, let's get you changed.

285
00:18:24,645 --> 00:18:30,818
[MUSIC BUILDING UP]

286
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:37,699
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:18:48,043 --> 00:18:50,671
Stay alert. We received a tip
from Benilda Cariño.

288
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:53,215
Someone might try to help
Mariela Mercado escape.

289
00:18:53,298 --> 00:18:54,967
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:56,635
Let's search the area. You take that side.

291
00:18:56,718 --> 00:18:58,387
- I'll take this one.
- Okay.

292
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,355
[GRUNTING]

293
00:19:09,565 --> 00:19:15,821
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

294
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:36,800
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

295
00:19:54,818 --> 00:19:55,652
<i>Sir?</i>

296
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:58,238
[BILLY GASPS]

297
00:19:58,322 --> 00:19:59,156
<i>Billy.</i>

298
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:03,619
- [LOUD THWACK]
- [MARIELA EXCLAIMS]

299
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:05,662
- [MARIELA SCREAMS]
- [CALOY GRUNTS]

300
00:20:05,746 --> 00:20:06,747
<i>- No!</i>
- [EXCLAIMS]

301
00:20:07,789 --> 00:20:08,665
<i>Mariela, no!</i>

302
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:09,875
[GRUNTING]

303
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:28,894
<i>Caloy, Caloy, Caloy, Caloy.</i>

304
00:20:28,977 --> 00:20:31,188
<i>Caloy. Caloy!</i>

305
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:33,315
- [TIRES SCREECH]
<i>- Caloy!</i>

306
00:20:33,398 --> 00:20:34,358
<i>Caloy!</i>

307
00:20:34,983 --> 00:20:36,026
<i>Caloy…</i>

308
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:37,653
[GASPS]

309
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:39,196
<i>Caloy.</i>

310
00:20:40,864 --> 00:20:41,907
<i>Caloy.</i>

311
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:47,371
<i>Caloy.</i>

312
00:20:52,251 --> 00:20:53,377
<i>'Bi…</i>

313
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:56,171
<i>Help me.</i>

314
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:57,923
<i>I don't want to die.</i>

315
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:01,134
<i>Die? What do you mean?</i>

316
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,011
<i>No one's going to die.</i>

317
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:04,513
<i>You're not going to die!</i>

318
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:06,890
<i>- You can't die.</i>
<i>- I don't want to.</i>

319
00:21:06,974 --> 00:21:09,601
<i>When will those other two</i>
<i>get their karma?</i>

320
00:21:10,811 --> 00:21:11,979
<i>It's taking forever.</i>

321
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:18,318
<i>Bea hasn't returned to the apartment.</i>

322
00:21:18,402 --> 00:21:20,237
<i>Do you think something happened</i>
<i>to your sister?</i>

323
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,363
[CHAIR SCRAPING]

324
00:21:21,446 --> 00:21:22,781
<i>What do you think, Dad?</i>

325
00:21:22,864 --> 00:21:26,201
<i>She's probably gone into hiding</i>
<i>with Mariela!</i>

326
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:27,828
<i>- Billy.</i>
<i>- Enrico.</i>

327
00:21:27,911 --> 00:21:29,746
<i>Try calling your place first.</i>

328
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,290
<i>Maybe she's there.</i>
